  "review": {
    "book": "2SA",
    "entityID": "person:abner_57",
    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "2SA2:8",
        "textualBasisJa": "Now Abner the son of Ner, captain of Saul’s army, had taken Ishbosheth the son of Saul and brought him over to Mahanaim."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA2:12",
        "textualBasisJa": "Abner the son of Ner, and the servants of Ishbosheth the son of Saul, went out from Mahanaim to Gibeon."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA2:14",
        "textualBasisJa": "Abner said to Joab, “Please let the young men arise and compete before us!” Joab said, “Let them arise!”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA2:17",
        "textualBasisJa": "The battle was very severe that day; and Abner was beaten, and the men of Israel, before David’s servants."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA2:19",
        "textualBasisJa": "Asahel pursued Abner. He didn’t turn to the right hand or to the left from following Abner."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA2:20",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then Abner looked behind him and said, “Is that you, Asahel?” He answered, “It is.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA2:21",
        "textualBasisJa": "Abner said to him, “Turn away to your right hand or to your left, and grab one of the young men, and take his armor.” But Asahel would not turn away from following him."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA2:22",
        "textualBasisJa": "Abner said again to Asahel, “Turn away from following me. Why should I strike you to the ground? How then could I look Joab your brother in the face?”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA2:23",
        "textualBasisJa": "However, he refused to turn away. Therefore Abner with the back end of the spear struck him in the body, so that the spear came out behind him; and he fell down there and died in the same place. As many as came to the place where Asahel fell down and died stood still."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA2:24",
        "textualBasisJa": "But Joab and Abishai pursued Abner. The sun went down when they had come to the hill of Ammah, that lies before Giah by the way of the wilderness of Gibeon."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA2:25",
        "textualBasisJa": "The children of Benjamin gathered themselves together after Abner and became one band, and stood on the top of a hill."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA2:26",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then Abner called to Joab, and said, “Shall the sword devour forever? Don’t you know that it will be bitterness in the latter end? How long will it be then, before you ask the people to return from following their brothers?”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA2:29",
        "textualBasisJa": "Abner and his men went all that night through the Arabah; and they passed over the Jordan, and went through all Bithron, and came to Mahanaim."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA2:30",
        "textualBasisJa": "Joab returned from following Abner; and when he had gathered all the people together, nineteen men of David’s and Asahel were missing."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA2:31",
        "textualBasisJa": "But David’s servants had struck Benjamin and Abner’s men so that three hundred sixty men died."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA3:6",
        "textualBasisJa": "While there was war between Saul’s house and David’s house, Abner made himself strong in Saul’s house."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA3:7",
        "textualBasisJa": "Now Saul had a concubine, whose name was Rizpah, the daughter of Aiah; and Ishbosheth said to Abner, “Why have you gone in to my father’s concubine?”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA3:8",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then Abner was very angry about Ishbosheth’s words, and said, “Am I a dog’s head that belongs to Judah? Today I show kindness to your father Saul’s house, to his brothers, and to his friends, and have not delivered you into the hand of David; and yet you charge me today with a fault concerning this woman!"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA3:9",
        "textualBasisJa": "God do so to Abner, and more also, if, as the LORD has sworn to David, I don’t do even so to him:"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA3:11",
        "textualBasisJa": "He could not answer Abner another word, because he was afraid of him."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA3:12",
        "textualBasisJa": "Abner sent messengers to David on his behalf, saying, “Whose is the land?” and saying, “Make your alliance with me, and behold, my hand will be with you to bring all Israel around to you.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA3:16",
        "textualBasisJa": "Her husband went with her, weeping as he went, and followed her to Bahurim. Then Abner said to him, “Go! Return!” and he returned."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA3:17",
        "textualBasisJa": "Abner had communication with the elders of Israel, saying, “In times past, you sought for David to be king over you."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA3:19",
        "textualBasisJa": "Abner also spoke in the ears of Benjamin; and Abner went also to speak in the ears of David in Hebron all that seemed good to Israel and to the whole house of Benjamin."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA3:20",
        "textualBasisJa": "So Abner came to David to Hebron, and twenty men with him. David made Abner and the men who were with him a feast."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA3:21",
        "textualBasisJa": "Abner said to David, “I will arise and go, and will gather all Israel to my lord the king, that they may make a covenant with you, and that you may reign over all that your soul desires.” David sent Abner away; and he went in peace."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA3:22",
        "textualBasisJa": "Behold, David’s servants and Joab came from a raid and brought in a great plunder with them; but Abner was not with David in Hebron, for he had sent him away, and he had gone in peace."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA3:23",
        "textualBasisJa": "When Joab and all the army who was with him had come, they told Joab, “Abner the son of Ner came to the king, and he has sent him away, and he has gone in peace.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA3:24",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then Joab came to the king and said, “What have you done? Behold, Abner came to you. Why is it that you have sent him away, and he is already gone?"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA3:25",
        "textualBasisJa": "You know Abner the son of Ner. He came to deceive you, and to know your going out and your coming in, and to know all that you do.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA3:26",
        "textualBasisJa": "When Joab had come out from David, he sent messengers after Abner, and they brought him back from the well of Sirah; but David didn’t know it."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA3:27",
        "textualBasisJa": "When Abner had returned to Hebron, Joab took him aside into the middle of the gate to speak with him quietly, and struck him there in the body, so that he died for the blood of Asahel his brother."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA3:28",
        "textualBasisJa": "Afterward, when David heard it, he said, “I and my kingdom are guiltless before the LORD forever of the blood of Abner the son of Ner."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA3:30",
        "textualBasisJa": "So Joab and Abishai his brother killed Abner, because he had killed their brother Asahel at Gibeon in the battle."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA3:31",
        "textualBasisJa": "David said to Joab and to all the people who were with him, “Tear your clothes, and clothe yourselves with sackcloth, and mourn in front of Abner.” King David followed the bier."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA3:32",
        "textualBasisJa": "They buried Abner in Hebron; and the king lifted up his voice and wept at Abner’s grave; and all the people wept."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA3:33",
        "textualBasisJa": "The king lamented for Abner, and said, “Should Abner die as a fool dies?"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA3:37",
        "textualBasisJa": "So all the people and all Israel understood that day that it was not of the king to kill Abner the son of Ner."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA4:1",
        "textualBasisJa": "When Saul’s son heard that Abner was dead in Hebron, his hands became feeble, and all the Israelites were troubled."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2SA4:12",
        "textualBasisJa": "David commanded his young men, and they killed them, cut off their hands and their feet, and hanged them up beside the pool in Hebron. But they took the head of Ishbosheth and buried it in Abner’s grave in Hebron."
      }
    ],
